      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">1. Statutory Framework: Article 61-B and the AIMA Transition</h2>
        <p>
          Portugal codified its dedicated digital nomad immigration stream under <strong>Decreto Regulamentar n.º 4/2022</strong>, amending the landmark Foreigners Act (<em>Lei n.º 23/2007</em>) through the creation of Article 61-B. Prior to this statutory enactment, location-independent tech professionals frequently relied on the passive-income D7 visa or irregular Schengen tourist stays. The D8 regime established clear legal parameters for remote salaried employees (<em>trabalho subordinado</em>) and independent contractors (<em>trabalho independente</em>) servicing clients outside Portuguese territory.
        </p>
        <p>
          Administratively, the application lifecycle shifted drastically following the dissolution of the <em>Serviço de Estrangeiros e Fronteiras</em> (SEF) in late 2023. Immigration enforcement and card issuance were transferred to the <strong>Agência para a Integração, Migrações e Asilo (AIMA)</strong>. For 2026 applicants, this transition means consular stages are managed by VFS Global and regional Portuguese embassies, while biometric capture, physical residency permits, and renewals are scheduled via AIMA’s modernized digital queue systems.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">2. The 2026 4x SMN Income Proof Formula and Dependent Multipliers</h2>
        <p>
          The financial threshold for the D8 visa is indexed directly to the Portuguese statutory minimum wage (<em>Salário Mínimo Nacional</em> - SMN). By council decree, the 2026 baseline SMN is set at <strong>€870 per month</strong> (paid across 14 statutory cycles, or annualized to €12,180).
        </p>
        <p>
          Under Article 61-B, paragraph 2, the primary applicant must demonstrate that their average monthly earnings across the preceding three calendar months equal or exceed <strong>400% (4x) of the monthly SMN</strong>:
        </p>
        
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs my-4 text-slate-300">
          <p class="text-amber-400 font-bold mb-1">// Portuguese D8 Statutory Income Formula (2026)</p>
          <p>Solo Applicant: 4 × €870 = <span class="text-white font-bold">€3,480.00 / month</span> (€41,760.00 / year)</p>
          <p>Spousal Supplement (+50% SMN): +0.50 × €870 = <span class="text-white font-bold">+€435.00 / month</span></p>
          <p>Child Supplement (+30% SMN): +0.30 × €870 = <span class="text-white font-bold">+€261.00 / month</span></p>
        </div>

        <p>
          When submitting evidentiary documentation, consular officers do not accept future projections or speculative equity valuations. Applicants must submit official bank statements detailing inbound transactions matching issued client invoices or payroll paystubs, accompanied by a letter of active employment or multi-month client service contracts.
        </p>

