      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">3. Bank Account Architecture: NIF Acquisition & Proof of Capital Deposit</h2>
        <p>
          A frequent cause of administrative rejection at VFS and consular triage is the lack of a fully funded Portuguese banking account. Even if an applicant earns €10,000 monthly, Portuguese administrative law insists on local liquid solvency.
        </p>
        <p>
          The procedural chain requires three deterministic steps:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Tax Identification Number (NIF):</strong> Non-EU residents must obtain a <em>Número de Identificação Fiscal</em> via an authorized fiscal representative (<em>representante fiscal</em>) or through digital registration platforms authenticated with Portuguese tax authorities (<em>Autoridade Tributária e Aduaneira</em>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Portuguese Bank Account Opening:</strong> Establish an account with a Tier-1 Portuguese retail bank (e.g., Millennium BCP, Novo Banco, Caixa Geral de Depósitos, or Banco Santander Totta). Opening can be executed remotely via Power of Attorney (<em>Procuração</em>) or biometric video verification.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Capital Transfer (12x SMN Minimum):</strong> Fund the account with a minimum lump-sum of €10,440 for solo applicants (€15,660 if co-applying with a spouse). Obtain a formal signed statement of balance (<em>Declaração de Saldo</em>) stamped by the bank branch dated within 30 days of submission.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">4. Accommodation Proof: Registered Leases vs Atestado de Residência</h2>
        <p>
          Consular posts strictly evaluate whether the nomad has stable, legally documented shelter. Short-term Airbnb or booking confirmations exceeding 30 days are routinely rejected for the Residency Visa track.
        </p>
        <p>
          Valid instruments accepted by AIMA include:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Contrato de Arrendamento com Registo nas Finanças:</strong> A minimum 12-month residential lease signed by both tenant and landlord, accompanied by the proof of registration stamp from the Portuguese Tax Authority (<em>Comprovativo de Registo de Contrato de Arrendamento no Portal das Finanças</em>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Escritura Pública de Compra e Venda:</strong> Deed of property purchase in Portugal registered with the Land Registry (<em>Conservatória do Registo Predial</em>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Termo de Responsabilidade:</strong> A formal affidavit of accommodation issued by a Portuguese citizen or legal permanent resident, supplemented by their certified tax return and property deed.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Atestado de Residência:</strong> Issued by the local civil parish (<em>Junta de Freguesia</em>) confirming that the individual physically resides at the designated local address, typically corroborated by two registered local voters.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">5. Tax Structuring: NHR Sunset, IFICI (NHR 2.0) and Progressive IRS Rates</h2>
        <p>
          Following the formal closure of the original Non-Habitual Resident (NHR) 20% flat tax regime in December 2023, incoming 2026 digital nomads must navigate updated tax architectures. Under general Portuguese Personal Income Tax (<em>Imposto sobre o Rendimento das Pessoas Singulares</em> - IRS), tax residents are subject to progressive brackets starting at 13.25% and scaling rapidly up to 48% (plus a solidarity surcharge of 2.5% to 5% on earnings above €80,000).
        </p>
        <p>
          Nomads qualifying under the new <strong>Tax Incentive for Scientific Research and Innovation (IFICI)</strong>—often termed NHR 2.0—can secure a 20% flat rate if their remote services fall into high-tech, certified research, or qualifying startup innovation codes approved by IAPMEI or AICEP. Those outside eligible innovation codes must optimize through deductible professional expenses under the simplified accounting regime (<em>Regime Simplificado</em>), where 25% of gross freelance service income is automatically recognized as operating expenses, taxing only 75% of net revenues.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">6. Automated Compliance Verification Script: Financial & Document Audit</h2>
        <p>
          Before scheduling consular review, legal teams and applicants can run this automated Python validation script to cross-examine foreign currency fluctuations, minimum wage ratios, and file readiness:
        </p>

<pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono overflow-x-auto text-emerald-400">
import sys
from decimal import Decimal

def verify_portugal_d8_eligibility(
    monthly_gross_eur: Decimal,
    bank_balance_eur: Decimal,
    adult_dependents: int = 0,
    minor_dependents: int = 0,
    has_nif: bool = False,
    lease_registered_financas: bool = False,
    criminal_check_apostilled: bool = False
) -> dict:
    SMN_2026 = Decimal("870.00")
    
    # Calculate statutory requirements
    base_required_income = SMN_2026 * Decimal("4.0")
    adult_supp = Decimal(adult_dependents) * (SMN_2026 * Decimal("0.50"))
    child_supp = Decimal(minor_dependents) * (SMN_2026 * Decimal("0.30"))
    total_required_income = base_required_income + adult_supp + child_supp
    
    # Bank savings requirements (12 months SMN)
    base_savings = SMN_2026 * Decimal("12.0")
    adult_savings = Decimal(adult_dependents) * (SMN_2026 * Decimal("6.0"))
    child_savings = Decimal(minor_dependents) * (SMN_2026 * Decimal("3.6"))
    total_required_savings = base_savings + adult_savings + child_savings
    
    income_pass = monthly_gross_eur >= total_required_income
    savings_pass = bank_balance_eur >= total_required_savings
    docs_pass = has_nif and lease_registered_financas and criminal_check_apostilled
    
    return {
        "status": "APPROVED" if (income_pass and savings_pass and docs_pass) else "DISQUALIFIED",
        "monthly_income_submitted": float(monthly_gross_eur),
        "monthly_income_required": float(total_required_income),
        "income_ratio": float(monthly_gross_eur / total_required_income),
        "savings_submitted": float(bank_balance_eur),
        "savings_required": float(total_required_savings),
        "critical_flags": {
            "income_deficit": float(max(Decimal(0), total_required_income - monthly_gross_eur)),
            "savings_deficit": float(max(Decimal(0), total_required_savings - bank_balance_eur)),
            "missing_nif": not has_nif,
            "unregistered_lease": not lease_registered_financas,
            "missing_apostille": not criminal_check_apostilled
        }
    }

if __name__ == "__main__":
    audit = verify_portugal_d8_eligibility(
        monthly_gross_eur=Decimal("3800.00"),
        bank_balance_eur=Decimal("12000.00"),
        adult_dependents=1,
        minor_dependents=0,
        has_nif=True,
        lease_registered_financas=True,
        criminal_check_apostilled=True
    )
    print(f"Pre-Flight Result: {audit['status']}")
    print(f"Income Margin: {audit['income_ratio'] * 100:.1f}% of threshold")
</pre>
